  "description": "QECTAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H68 Dy4 N14 Ni5 O36,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni7 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni8 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni9 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni10 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.360-4.372 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.38-119.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H68Dy4N14Ni5O36·C2H3N.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
